---

The above covers the code SpiceSee's authors wrote. This repository also
contains third-party code under its own terms:

  * Packages/CSpiceCodec/Sources/CSpiceCodec/vendor/ holds SPICE image
    codecs copied from spice-common and spice-gtk, licensed
    LGPL-2.1-or-later, plus headers from spice-protocol under the
    BSD-3-Clause licence. Each file carries its own licence header, and
    Packages/CSpiceCodec/Sources/CSpiceCodec/VENDORED.md records every
    file with its upstream origin and revision. The CSpiceCodec.framework
    built from those sources remains LGPL-2.1-or-later when distributed;
    docs/replacing-the-codec.md describes how to substitute your own
    build of it.

  * Sources/SpiceSee/Licenses/ holds the licence texts shown in the app's
    acknowledgements window: LGPL-2.1, BSD-3-Clause (spice-protocol) and
    MIT (Sparkle).
